(ns png.grammar
  "resources/png/grammar.edn as a value, for callers that have no classpath
  resource loader.

  `png.core/parse` takes the grammar as an argument, and the only way this
  repository offered it was `resources/png/grammar.edn` -- which a JVM caller
  reads with `io/resource` and a caller under kbb (ClojureScript on Node) can
  only read by guessing a path relative to its working directory. A library
  that decodes PNGs on behalf of somebody else (kotoba-lang/image) has no
  such directory to guess. This namespace is the same data, requireable.

  The resource file stays the source of truth: png.grammar-test reads it and
  asserts it is equal to `grammar`, on both runtimes, so the two cannot drift
  without a red test.")

(def grammar
  {:meta  {:id :png :endian :big :root :png-file}

   :enums {:color-type {0 :gray 2 :rgb 3 :indexed 4 :gray-alpha 6 :rgba}}

   :types
   {:png-file
    [{:id :sig    :type :bytes :size 8}
     {:id :chunks :type :seq :until-eof true :of :chunk}]

    :chunk
    [{:id :length :type :u32}
     {:id :type   :type :str  :size 4}
     {:id :data   :type :bytes :size [:field :length]}
     {:id :crc    :type :u32}]

    :ihdr
    [{:id :width       :type :u32}
     {:id :height      :type :u32}
     {:id :bit-depth   :type :u8}
     {:id :color-type  :type :u8 :enum :color-type}
     {:id :compression :type :u8}
     {:id :filter      :type :u8}
     {:id :interlace   :type :u8}]}})
